-- title:
--   Branch exchange carries the ideal (U) onto (V)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Write $R_\pi$ for the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W π`, that is, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W π` generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - \pi$ (the constant $\pi$ being included via `MvPowerSeries.C`). Let `crossingSwap π` be the ring automorphism of $R_\pi$ obtained by descending to the quotient the ring isomorphism `uvSwapEquiv` of $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ that renames the variables along the transposition of $0$ and $1$ in $\mathrm{Fin}\ 2$; this descent is legitimate because that renaming sends `uvCrossingIdeal W π` to itself. The statement concerns the two distinguished elements `U π` and `V π` of $R_\pi$, which the swap interchanges in the sense that `crossingSwap π (U π) = V π`. The assertion is an equality of ideals of $R_\pi$: the image under `crossingSwap π` of the principal ideal generated by `U π`, formed as `Ideal.map`, is equal to the principal ideal generated by `V π`.
--
--   This is the ideal-theoretic form of the statement that the involution exchanging the two coordinates of the local crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ interchanges its two branches — the local picture at a supersingular point of the special fibre of $X_0(p)$, where the Atkin–Lehner involution exchanges the two irreducible components. It is used in [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_span_U_quotient_span_V`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_span_U_quotient_span_V), which produces from it a ring isomorphism between the two branch quotients.
